# Project Information
project_name: "cursor-demo"
frontend: "cursor-demo/bacmy-app"
backend_stack: react and material ui

# Branch Naming Convention
When creating git branches, always use this format:
- feature/{TICKET-ID}-{brief-kebab-case-description}
- bugfix/{TICKET-ID}-{brief-kebab-case-description}
- hotfix/{TICKET-ID}-{brief-kebab-case-description}

Examples:
- feature/PROJ-123-user-analytics-dashboard
- bugfix/PROJ-456-fix-login-redirect
- hotfix/PROJ-789-critical-security-patch

# Commit Message Structure
All commit messages must follow this format:
{TICKET-ID}: {type}: {description}

Types (use exactly these):
- feat: New feature
- fix: Bug fix
- refactor: Code refactoring without functionality change
- docs: Documentation changes
- test: Adding or updating tests
- style: Code style changes (formatting, missing semicolons, etc.)
- chore: Maintenance tasks, dependency updates
- perf: Performance improvements

Examples:
- PROJ-123: feat: add user analytics dashboard with real-time metrics
- PROJ-456: fix: resolve login redirect loop on session timeout
- PROJ-789: refactor: extract authentication logic into custom hook
- PROJ-234: test: add unit tests for UserMetrics component

# Pull Request Requirements
When creating pull requests:

Title format: [{TICKET-ID}] {Brief description}
Example: [PROJ-123] User Analytics Dashboard

Description template:

Description
{Brief overview of changes}
Changes Made

{Change 1}
{Change 2}
{Change 3}

Related Ticket
Jira: TICKET-ID

Target branch: production